# Done bar — last hop live

A slice, todo, or “implemented” claim is **done** only when the designed path is wired end-to-end: the real caller uses it, and the real call site exists in the product tree.

If the last hop is missing, the first sentence to Rodrigo is that it is **incomplete**. Do **not** mark the todo complete. Do **not** say implemented / fechado / pronto.

## Not done (this is the error)

- Encoder, helper, or ABI exists but the live consumer still uses another path (JSON, fake mouse, dead export).
- IPDL / Runtime handler exists but nothing in Gecko/Firefox source emits or waits (Python splice on checkout is not a call site).
- Unit / golden / FakeBrowser parse green while the product path is unwired.
- Files on disk + compile-shaped C++ with a guessed API.
- “The pipe exists” / “ready for mach” while join-or-open, coords, or hooks are still stubs.

## Done

- Grep shows the production/lab caller hitting the new path (not a sibling unused module).
- Native hook lives in the patch/source tree at the real function (`alert`, permission, download, channel), not a checkout script.
- Asset/input/nav apply the designed algorithm (join the page channel; convert coords; no NullPrincipal second GET).
- If effect still needs one rebuild: say **wired, unproven** — never **done**. Unproven is allowed. Unwired is not.

## Duty

Finish the last hop before the next slice. Covering every todo with envelopes is a product defect.
